<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wars of Alexander the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">336–323 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Conquests of Alexander the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wars of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> were the campaigns fought by Alexander III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> between 336 and 323 BCE, first to secure <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and then against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Persian Empire</a>. Victories at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-granicus">Granicus</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-issus">Issus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela">Gaugamela</a> gave him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, and he pressed on through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> valley. His conquests spread Greek rule and culture across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a> and opened the Hellenistic age.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wars-of-alexander-the-great.jpg" alt="Wars of Alexander the Great" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_the_Great_mosaic.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
